Inspired by the Tournament, I thought I'd try ascending all the classes
- just quick and dirty ascensions, with whatever lessons I learn along
the way.  Hence my Yet Another Bunch of Ascension Posts.

First one: Valere A2-Arc-Neu-Hum-Fem

This one went fairly easily.  Valere A1 died because she wasn't
watching her hit points, but generally, starting with speed, a
touchstone, and a pickaxe is a pretty good set.

Valere A2 switched to her pickaxe immediately, and picked up dwarven
armor and a mattock by the time she reached minetown.  She finished the
mines without finding a magic lamp, then moved on.  If I had it to do
over again, I would probably drop to minetown, then climb back up and
do Sokoban.  The risk of death by wand in the final few levels was too
much.

The rest was pretty simple.  Valere cleared the castle, wished for
Greyswandir, her ascension kit, the orb of fate, and spellbooks of ID
and MM, finished the quest, then finished things off.
Lessons learned:  (1) Watch your hitpoints.  (2) Use your speed.


